ErbB receptor family: a therapeutic target for cancer</article-title><source>Trends Mol Med</source><year>2002</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>S19</fpage><lpage>S26</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Trends Mol Med||8|S19||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11927283</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Droller</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bladder cancer: state-of-the-art care</article-title><source>CA Cancer J Clin</source><year>1998</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>269</fpage><lpage>284</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'CA Cancer J Clin||48|269||bib14|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9742894</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Earp</surname><given-names>HS</given-names><suffix>3rd</suffix></name><name><surname>Calvo</surname><given-names>BF</given-names></name><name><surname>Sartor</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The EGF receptor family &#x02013; multiple roles in proliferation, differentiation, and neoplasia with an emphasis on HER4</article-title><source>Trans Am Clin Climatol Assoc</source><year>2003</year><volume>114</volume><fpage>315</fpage><lpage>333</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Trans Am Clin Climatol Assoc||114|315||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12813928</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gullick</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Type 1 growth factor receptors and their ligands considered as a complex system</article-title><source>Endocr Relat Cancer</source><year>2001</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>75</fpage><lpage>82</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Endocr Relat Cancer||8|75||bib16|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11397665</pub-id><